1
00:00:00,909 --> 00:00:01,989
(Raj:)Oh, snap.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,200
[CHUCKLES]

3
00:00:03,369 --> 00:00:04,409
(Sheldon:)Snap what?

4
00:00:05,497 --> 00:00:08,287
- Okay, I guess we have to turn to plan B.
- What's plan B?

5
00:00:08,458 --> 00:00:13,088
Erase the hard drives, grab the tapes, wipe
our fingerprints off every surface and run.

6
00:00:13,254 --> 00:00:14,964
(Sheldon:)Why wasn't that plan A?

7
00:00:17,675 --> 00:00:20,595
ANNOUNCER [ON TV]: A NASA spokesman
states that due to the loss of data...

8
00:00:20,762 --> 00:00:23,602
...they will most likely be unable
to determine the cause...

9
00:00:23,765 --> 00:00:26,435
...of the Mars rover's malfunction.

10
00:00:28,686 --> 00:00:31,316
(Howard:)Thank God for plan B.

11
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:34,855
(Penny:)Howard, didn't you say
you worked on the Mars rover?

12
00:00:35,026 --> 00:00:37,236
(Howard:)No, you're mistaken.

13
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:38,950
(Penny:)Yeah, when we first met.

14
00:00:39,113 --> 00:00:42,113
(Penny:)You said that if I went out with you
I could drive a car on Mars.

15
00:00:44,577 --> 00:00:47,617
(Howard:)I don't know what you're talking about.

16
00:00:47,789 --> 00:00:49,419
LEONARD:
Psst?

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,130
(Sheldon:)Will you all excuse me?

18
00:00:52,293 --> 00:00:57,023
Leonard is signaling
that he'd like to talk to me in private.

